00:22:41.940 --> 00:22:43.860
But that's what the government counts on.

00:22:44.060 --> 00:22:47.500
They do they do a couple of things on purpose.

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:52.780
One is called charge stacking, where they'll charge you with a whole bunch of felonies.

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.980
You know, felonies, you haven't committed.

00:22:55.180 --> 00:22:58.100
And then they'll wait until you go bankrupt.

00:22:58.300 --> 00:23:01.780
And then they'll come back and say, hey, we'll drop all the charges,

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:03.780
but one, if you take a plea.

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:05.860
And by then you have no hope.

00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:10.100
You're ruined financially, professionally, personally in many cases.

00:23:10.340 --> 00:23:12.140
And so you take the plea.

00:23:12.340 --> 00:23:18.460
This is why ProPublica found in a study that the government wins 98.2 percent

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:22.900
of its cases, almost all of those wins are because of plea bargains.

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:25.740
And the other thing they do is venue shopping.

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:31.140
Yeah, they want they want to bring a case against you in the federal

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:35.940
district where they know they have the best chance of winning.

